       "text": "I won't enter this order. No indication supports sertraline 1000 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 200 mg/day, and a dose this high puts the patient at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. I can't verify the clinical rationale from here. Even with a confirmation, I can't enter an order that is this far past the safe limit without a safeguard.\n\nYou have a few options:\n\n- **Order a dose within range.** I can enter sertraline at up to 200 mg once daily right now.\n- **Go through pharmacy and the attending.** If there is a documented rationale, such as a specialist recommendation, the order should be reviewed and entered through your hospital's high-dose override process. That process typically needs pharmacist verification and prescriber co-signature.\n- **Check for an error.** If the intended drug or dose was different, tell me and I'll enter the corrected order.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
